<title>FRANCE: Tayfunair stops London-Maastricht-Istanbul service.</title>
<headline>Tayfunair stops London-Maastricht-Istanbul service.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tayfunair has stopped its twice-weekly Boeing 727 freighter service to and from London to Istanbul via Maastricht, the Turkish airline's French cargo sales agent, Air Cargo Logistics (ACL), told Reuters.</p>
<p>&quot;The service was suspended around the beginning of the month and followed a strategic decision by Tayfunair's shareholders in Turkey to pull out of the air transport sector which they judged was not profitable enough,&quot; an ACL official said.</p>
<p>ACL trucked around 15 tonnes of freight to Maastricht each week with capacity also shared with GSA's in the Benelux and Germany, the official added.</p>
<p>&quot;The service performed very well with the 22-tonne capacity 727F often leaving full.&quot; -- Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax+5017</p>
</text>
